# One fresh process per (size, engine): FASTPOSTGRES_TRANSPORT is read at
# import and a ring's engine is fixed at creation, so a process cannot serve
# both engines. The adbc players do not depend on it: they are measured once
# per size (in the first engine's process) and recorded once.
# The table per size puts the three families side by side; every fastpostgres
# record also carries the cell's ring evidence - the rings the cell left in
# /dev/shm all name the engine, and the harness's own probe read was served by
# the ring (served_by_shm 1/1) with the same digest in every cell.
### END ENV

